%description:

Tcp.advertisedWindow:scaled -- the SYN-ACK offers 65535, and the later ACKs a scaled window above 65535.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the receive window that this host offers, in bytes; ... above 65535 it
needs window scaling, and a SYN or a SYN-ACK offers at most 65535, because its window is not
scaled (RFC 7323 section 2.2)".

The classes: unscaled (65535 and less: the default, and 14 * 536 = 7504 of LegacyTcp), scaled
(above 65535, with window scaling), unscalable (above 65535 without window scaling: an error),
too-large (above 65535 << 14 = 1073725440: an error). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks the value and sets the first offer;
TcpConnection::synWindow() limits the window of a SYN to 65535; the window scale of the
connection carries a larger window. This test separates "scaled" from "unscaled".

Host under test: host2, the server, which receives 1000000 bytes. Observation: level 1, the
SYN-ACK of host2 offers 65535 bytes; level 2, the send window of host1 (the signal sndWnd)
grows above 200000 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.advertisedWindow
%# class: scaled
%# value: 262144
%# key: *.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAdvertisedWindowScaled")
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.window == 65535")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("sndWnd")
                  .filterValueAtLeast(200000)
                  .describe("the send window of host1: the scaled offer of host2")
                  .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAdvertisedWindowScaled compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 262144    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAdvertisedWindowScaled: PASS
